libjuice 3c40a354: give each TURN allocation back when an agent is destroyed

NereusSDR for iOS patch, applied by ios/scripts/vendor-sources.sh libjuice after
it copies the pinned archive's files. MPL-2.0, like the file it changes: the
change becomes part of src/agent.c, a covered file, so it is available under
MPL-2.0 (section 3.1), and the modified file is published with NereusSDR's
source. iPhone app plan Task 28a (R-IOS-16), 2026-09-27.

libjuice never gives a TURN allocation back: when a connection ends, the relay
holds the allocation, and one place in the per-user quota of the Core's id
(eight since 2026-09-26), for the rest of its lifetime, TURN_LIFETIME, ten
minutes. A phone that reconnects through the relay after a network change
could then find no place left for its new allocations. The link document
("Control over a data channel") has each end give its allocations back at
once when a connection ends, with a Refresh whose LIFETIME is 0 (RFC 8656
section 7.2); the desktop and the Core make the same change to the same
libjuice (cmake/NereusRemoteMedia.cmake).

When an agent is destroyed, before its connection is, each relay entry the
relay granted (succeeded, with a relayed address and the nonce of the relay's
authentication) gets one Refresh with LIFETIME 0, signed with the entry's own
credentials, sent once and not retransmitted: a lost one leaves the
allocation to expire as before. Nothing else changes.

--- a/src/agent.c
+++ b/src/agent.c
@@ -157,6 +157,47 @@
 	return NULL;
 }
 
+// NereusSDR (iPhone app plan Task 28a): gives each TURN allocation this agent holds back to its
+// relay with a Refresh whose LIFETIME is 0 (RFC 8656 section 7.2), so the relay's per-user quota
+// is free at once rather than for the rest of the allocation's lifetime. Sent once and not
+// retransmitted: an allocation whose release is lost expires as it did before.
+static void agent_give_back_turn_allocations(juice_agent_t *agent) {
+	if (!agent->conn_impl)
+		return;
+
+	conn_lock(agent);
+	for (int i = 0; i < agent->entries_count; ++i) {
+		const agent_stun_entry_t *entry = agent->entries + i;
+		if (entry->type != AGENT_STUN_ENTRY_TYPE_RELAY || !entry->turn)
+			continue;
+
+		// Only an allocation the relay granted, which has a relayed address and the nonce the
+		// relay's authentication gave
+		bool granted = entry->state == AGENT_STUN_ENTRY_STATE_SUCCEEDED ||
+		               entry->state == AGENT_STUN_ENTRY_STATE_SUCCEEDED_KEEPALIVE;
+		if (!granted || entry->relayed.len == 0 || *entry->turn->credentials.nonce == '\0')
+			continue;
+
+		stun_message_t msg;
+		memset(&msg, 0, sizeof(msg));
+		msg.msg_class = STUN_CLASS_REQUEST;
+		msg.msg_method = STUN_METHOD_REFRESH;
+		juice_random(msg.transaction_id, STUN_TRANSACTION_ID_SIZE);
+		msg.lifetime = 0;
+		msg.lifetime_set = true;
+		msg.credentials = entry->turn->credentials;
+
+		char buffer[BUFFER_SIZE];
+		int size = stun_write(buffer, BUFFER_SIZE, &msg, entry->turn->password);
+		if (size <= 0 || agent_direct_send(agent, &entry->record, buffer, size, 0) < 0) {
+			JLOG_WARN("Could not give a TURN allocation back");
+			continue;
+		}
+		JLOG_DEBUG("Gave a TURN allocation back");
+	}
+	conn_unlock(agent);
+}
+
 void agent_destroy(juice_agent_t *agent) {
 	JLOG_DEBUG("Destroying agent");
 
@@ -164,6 +205,8 @@
 		JLOG_VERBOSE("Waiting for resolver thread");
 		thread_join(agent->resolver_thread, NULL);
 	}
+
+	agent_give_back_turn_allocations(agent);
 
 	if (agent->conn_impl) {
 		conn_destroy(agent);
